{
  "info": {
    "name": "Advanced Educational RAG API",
    "description": "Postman collection for the Advanced Educational RAG API.\n\n=== SETUP ===\n1. Import this collection into Postman\n2. Set the 'base_url' collection variable (default: http://localhost:8000)\n3. Start services:\n   - docker-compose up -d qdrant redis\n   - ollama serve\n   - uvicorn src.api.app:app --reload --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000\n\n=== RECOMMENDED FLOW ===\n1. GET  /health             — verify all services are up\n2. POST /session            — create a session, session_id auto-saved to variable\n3. POST /query              — ask a question using {{session_id}}\n4. GET  /session/{id}       — inspect full chat history\n5. POST /session/{id}/clear — reset history but keep session\n6. DELETE /session/{id}     — delete session entirely\n\n=== COLLECTIONS ===\n- 'pdf'   → PDF chunks only  (citations: filename + page number)\n- 'audio' → Audio transcripts only (citations: title + start/end time)\n- omit    → Search both collections\n\n=== TIPS ===\n- session_id is returned in every /query response\n- Pass the same session_id in follow-up queries for memory\n- use_self_reflection=false for faster responses\n- top_k default 10, max 50",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "base_url",
      "value": "http://localhost:8000",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Base URL of the RAG API. Change if running on a different host/port."
    },
    {
      "key": "session_id",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Active session ID. Auto-populated by the Create Session request."
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "1. Health",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Health Check",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/health",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["health"]
            },
            "description": "Check if Qdrant and Ollama are reachable.\n\nExpected response:\n{\n  \"status\": \"ok\",\n  \"qdrant\": true,\n  \"ollama\": true,\n  \"details\": null\n}\n\nIf status is 'degraded', check the details field for which service is down."
          },
          "response": [
            {
              "name": "200 OK — All services up",
              "status": "OK",
              "code": 200,
              "header": [{"key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json"}],
              "body": "{\n  \"status\": \"ok\",\n  \"qdrant\": true,\n  \"ollama\": true,\n  \"details\": null\n}"
            },
            {
              "name": "200 OK — Degraded (Ollama down)",
              "status": "OK",
              "code": 200,
              "header": [{"key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json"}],
              "body": "{\n  \"status\": \"degraded\",\n  \"qdrant\": true,\n  \"ollama\": false,\n  \"details\": {\n    \"ollama_error\": \"Connection refused\"\n  }\n}"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Root",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": [""]
            },
            "description": "Root endpoint — confirms API is running."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Swagger Docs",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/docs",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["docs"]
            },
            "description": "Open Swagger UI in browser for interactive API documentation."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "2. Session",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Create Session",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "var json = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (json.session_id) {",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('session_id', json.session_id);",
                  "    console.log('session_id saved:', json.session_id);",
                  "    pm.test('Session created successfully', function() {",
                  "        pm.expect(json.session_id).to.be.a('string');",
                  "        pm.expect(json.session_id.length).to.be.above(0);",
                  "    });",
                  "}"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/session",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["session"]
            },
            "description": "Create a new chat session in Redis.\n\nThe session_id is automatically saved to the {{session_id}} collection variable.\nUse this session_id in all /query requests to maintain conversation memory.\n\nSessions expire after inactivity (default TTL: 1 hour)."
          },
          "response": [
            {
              "name": "201 Created",
              "status": "Created",
              "code": 201,
              "header": [{"key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json"}],
              "body": "{\n  \"session_id\": \"a1b2c3d4-e5f6-7890-abcd-ef1234567890\",\n  \"message\": \"Session created successfully.\"\n}"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Get Session Info",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/session/{{session_id}}",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["session", "{{session_id}}"]
            },
            "description": "Get full chat history and metadata for a session.\n\nReturns:\n- exists: whether session is alive in Redis\n- history: list of all {role, content} turns\n- meta: created_at, last_active, query_count"
          },
          "response": [
            {
              "name": "200 OK — Session found",
              "status": "OK",
              "code": 200,
              "header": [{"key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json"}],
              "body": "{\n  \"session_id\": \"a1b2c3d4-e5f6-7890-abcd-ef1234567890\",\n  \"exists\": true,\n  \"history\": [\n    {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"What is biotechnology?\"},\n    {\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": \"Biotechnology is the use of biological systems...\"}\n  ],\n  \"meta\": {\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-05-31T10:00:00+00:00\",\n    \"last_active\": \"2026-05-31T10:05:00+00:00\",\n    \"query_count\": 1\n  }\n}"
            },
            {
              "name": "200 OK — Session not found / expired",
              "status": "OK",
              "code": 200,
              "header": [{"key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json"}],
              "body": "{\n  \"session_id\": \"a1b2c3d4-e5f6-7890-abcd-ef1234567890\",\n  \"exists\": false,\n  \"history\": [],\n  \"meta\": null\n}"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Clear Session History",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/session/{{session_id}}/clear",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["session", "{{session_id}}", "clear"]
            },
            "description": "Clear all chat history for the session but keep the session alive in Redis.\nUseful for starting a new topic without creating a new session."
          },
          "response": [
            {
              "name": "200 OK",
              "status": "OK",
              "code": 200,
              "header": [{"key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json"}],
              "body": "{\n  \"session_id\": \"a1b2c3d4-e5f6-7890-abcd-ef1234567890\",\n  \"message\": \"Session history cleared successfully.\"\n}"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Delete Session",
          "request": {
            "method": "DELETE",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/session/{{session_id}}",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["session", "{{session_id}}"]
            },
            "description": "Permanently delete a session and all its chat history from Redis.\n\nReturns 404 if session not found or already expired."
          },
          "response": [
            {
              "name": "200 OK",
              "status": "OK",
              "code": 200,
              "header": [{"key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json"}],
              "body": "{\n  \"session_id\": \"a1b2c3d4-e5f6-7890-abcd-ef1234567890\",\n  \"message\": \"Session deleted successfully.\"\n}"
            },
            {
              "name": "404 Not Found",
              "status": "Not Found",
              "code": 404,
              "header": [{"key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json"}],
              "body": "{\n  \"detail\": \"Session 'a1b2c3d4-...' not found or already expired.\"\n}"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "3. Query — PDF",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "PDF Query — Simple (No Session)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "var json = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (json.session_id) {",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('session_id', json.session_id);",
                  "    console.log('session_id updated:', json.session_id);",
                  "}",

                  "pm.test('Status 200', function() { pm.response.to.have.status(200); });",
                  "pm.test('has_answer field exists', function() { pm.expect(json).to.have.property('has_answer'); });",
                  "pm.test('cited_sources is array', function() { pm.expect(json.cited_sources).to.be.an('array'); });"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{"key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json"}],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"query\": \"What is biotechnology?\",\n  \"collection\": \"pdf\",\n  \"top_k\": 10,\n  \"use_self_reflection\": true\n}",
              "options": {"raw": {"language": "json"}}
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/query",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["query"]
            },
            "description": "Simple PDF query without a session.\nA new session is auto-created and session_id is returned + saved to collection variable.\n\nCitations will include PDF filename and page number where available."
          },
          "response": [
            {
              "name": "200 OK — PDF answer with citations",
              "status": "OK",
              "code": 200,
              "header": [{"key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json"}],
              "body": "{\n  \"answer\": \"Biotechnology is the use of biological systems, living organisms, or derivatives thereof to develop products and services [Source 1]. It includes applications in agriculture [Source 2] and medicine [Source 3].\",\n  \"cited_sources\": [\n    {\n      \"index\": 1,\n      \"source_type\": \"pdf\",\n      \"title\": \"10. Biotechnology and its Application.pdf\",\n      \"page\": 1,\n      \"start_time\": null,\n      \"end_time\": null,\n      \"preview\": \"Biotechnology essentially deals with industrial scale production...\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"cited_indices\": [1, 2, 3],\n  \"has_answer\": true,\n  \"iterations\": 1,\n  \"reflection\": {\n    \"overall_confidence\": 0.87,\n    \"accuracy_confidence\": 0.9,\n    \"completeness_confidence\": 0.85,\n    \"citation_confidence\": 0.88,\n    \"needs_more_retrieval\": false,\n    \"improvement_hint\": null,\n    \"uncertainties\": []\n  },\n  \"session_id\": \"a1b2c3d4-e5f6-7890-abcd-ef1234567890\"\n}"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "PDF Query — With Session (Memory)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "var json = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Status 200', function() { pm.response.to.have.status(200); });",
                  "pm.test('Answer returned', function() { pm.expect(json.answer).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty; });"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{"key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json"}],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"query\": \"What is biotechnology?\",\n  \"collection\": \"pdf\",\n  \"top_k\": 10,\n  \"use_self_reflection\": true,\n  \"session_id\": \"{{session_id}}\"\n}",
              "options": {"raw": {"language": "json"}}
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/query",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["query"]
            },
            "description": "PDF query using the active session from {{session_id}}.\nChat history is automatically loaded from Redis — no need to send chat_history manually.\n\nRun 'Create Session' first to populate {{session_id}}."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "PDF Query — Follow Up (Session Memory)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{"key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json"}],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"query\": \"What are its applications in agriculture?\",\n  \"collection\": \"pdf\",\n  \"top_k\": 10,\n  \"use_self_reflection\": true,\n  \"session_id\": \"{{session_id}}\"\n}",
              "options": {"raw": {"language": "json"}}
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/query",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["query"]
            },
            "description": "Follow-up question using session memory.\n'its' correctly resolves to biotechnology because the previous turn is loaded from Redis.\n\nNo need to manually pass chat_history — just pass the same session_id."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "PDF Query — No Self Reflection (Faster)",
          "request": {
